<http://data.silknow.org/object/98a8442c-4b4c-3b17-90ce-de237d5ccf01/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This boy's robe dates from a era when young boys in Europe wore garments with skirts, a custom with unclear origins, but which most likely had to do with making it easier for them to urinate. The style was common until about 1920. A boy usually received his first breeches or trousers between four and seven years of age, sometimes in a special ceremony held by the family."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/98a8442c-4b4c-3b17-90ce-de237d5ccf01> .

